  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Boiling Spring Lakes got its name from a spring that bubbles with pure water, discovered in a wooded ravine in 1961.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofbsl.org/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s centerpiece, the 275‑acre Big Lake, stretches 2½ miles long and boasts 10 miles of shoreline fed by five springs and Allen’s Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofbsl.org/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first development project, the Boiling Spring Dam, carved 10 miles of white‑sandy shoreline around what is now Patricia Lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ncplantfriends.org/042021bslhistory.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2018 Hurricane Florence wrecked the dam that held the main lake, prompting FEMA to fund repairs that are still underway as of June 2024.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boiling_Spring_Lakes%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Over 400 vascular plant species thrive in the Preserve, including rare plants like the federally listed rough‑leaf loosestrife and the Venus flytrap.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ncplantfriends.org/042021bslhistory.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Boiling Spring Lakes was officially incorporated as a town in 1961, the same year developers first found the gushing spring.",
